<title>JAPAN: Stock ratings list - Nomura Securities (Apr 9).</title>
<headline>Stock ratings list - Nomura Securities (Apr 9).</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Follows is a list of ratings on Wednesday by Nomura Securities Co Ltd.</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Rating unchanged:</p>
<p>Itochu Corp - &quot;1&quot;</p>
<p>Sekisui Chemical Co Ltd -- &quot;1&quot;</p>
<p>Aoyama Trading Co Ltd -- &quot;1&quot;</p>
<p>Tokyu Department Store Co Ltd -- &quot;2&quot;</p>
<p>Dowa Fire and Marine Insurance Co Ltd -- &quot;2&quot;</p>
<p>Nisshin Fire and Marine Insurance Co Ltd -- &quot;2&quot;</p>
<p>Nissan Fire and Marine Insurance Co Ltd -- &quot;2&quot;</p>
<p>Chiyoda Fire and Marine Insurance Co Ltd -- &quot;2&quot;</p>
<p>Matsushita Electric Works Ltd -- &quot;2&quot;</p>
<p>NTN Corp -- &quot;2&quot;</p>
<p>JGC Corp -- &quot;2&quot;</p>
<p>Daikin Industries Ltd -- &quot;2&quot;</p>
<p>Matsushita Seiko Co Ltd -- &quot;2&quot;</p>
<p>Zenrin Co Ltd -- &quot;2&quot;</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Nomura assigns ratings as follows:</p>
<p>&quot;1&quot; - issues expected to outperform the key 225-share Nikkei average by more than 10 percentage points over the following six months.</p>
<p>&quot;2&quot; - issues seen moving within 10 percentage points in either direction of the key 225-share Nikkei average over the next six months.</p>
<p>&quot;3&quot; - issues expected to underperform the key 225-share Nikkei average by more than 10 percentage points over the following six months.</p>
</text>
